Sparky Stereo OS: OpenSCAD 2026.11-RC1 (upstream tag openscad-2026.11-RC1, commit 2127234b), packaged for the edition: Debian testing has no OpenSCAD (bug 1149820 against the 2021 source) and SparkyLinux carries none. Packaging based on Debian's 2021.01-14 by Kristian Nielsen and Christian M. Amsüss, moved to CMake and Qt 6; Manifold v3.5.4 built from its submodule; the test suite not built.
The 3D view draws the preview and the rendered model as a stereo pair: two parallel cameras, an off-axis frustum in perspective and a shear in orthographic, into Qt's stereo buffers, which the edition's Qt gives the view as a stereo window of its own and the edition's Mesa hands to Stereo KWin as declared full side by side.
The separation is the person's depth limits, read from the desktop through libstereo-declare: the largest under which every pixel of the view stays inside them; no separation setting. Without limits both eyes are the same picture and the console says why, once.
The 3D options are Enable 3D (on by default, for new windows) and a button to Display Settings; the new sentences in the ten languages (translations/openscad-3d-view-stereo.po.patch).
Build-Depends on libstereo-declare-dev (>= 1.12.2) and Qt's private GUI headers (the window system's handles).
